desktop-shell-notification-daemon(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-notification-daemon - notification server with sounds, shown in the status bar

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-notification-daemon* [*-c* _FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION

*desktop-shell-notification-daemon* receives the notifications programs send
on the session bus (the Desktop Notifications Specification 1.2, bus name
_org.freedesktop.Notifications_). It shows nothing on screen: it plays a
sound, keeps the recent notifications and tells the status bar about them,
which shows the number of unread ones and the latest one, and brings up the
sender's window when clicked.

Sounds: a notification's own *sound-file* or *sound-name* hint plays when
given (the name is looked up in the freedesktop sound theme). A notification
with the *suppress-sound* hint plays nothing, as applications set it when
they play their own sound. Otherwise the daemon's chime plays, a more
insistent one for critical notifications. At most one sound plays per
*minimum-interval*, and none during do-not-disturb (critical ones aside, if
*critical-sounds* is true).

A notification counts as expired for its sender after its timeout; it stays
unread until the status bar marks it read. It follows the compositor through
_$SWAYSOCK_ to bring up windows and to reread its settings on *swaymsg
reload*, after which it also restarts from a newly installed file.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Accepted like by every component; unused, as nothing is drawn.

# STATUS BAR INTERFACE

On the same bus name, object
_/io/github/mrcingo/DesktopShellComponents/NotificationCenter_, interface
_io.github.mrcingo.DesktopShellComponents.NotificationCenter_:

*UnreadCount* (u, read)
	Notifications that arrived and were not read yet.

*LatestText* (s, read)
	The newest unread one as "Application: summary", at most 120 characters;
	empty when none is unread.

*LatestUrgency* (y, read)
	Its urgency: 0 low, 1 normal, 2 critical.

*DoNotDisturb* (b, read and write)

*ActivateLatest()*
	Brings up the newest unread notification's window: the sender's process
	window, else its parent's (a terminal running a script), else its
	child's, else a window with the application's name. Then sends the
	sender the "default" action if it offered one, and marks it read.

*MarkAllRead()*, *ToggleDoNotDisturb()*

Every property change is announced with PropertiesChanged.

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/notification-daemon.ini_,
else _@sysconfdir@/xdg/desktop-shell-components/notification-daemon.ini_,
which lists every setting with its default. All are optional; *swaymsg
reload* applies changes, except the history size, which applies on restart.

*[sound]*
	*play-sound* = _unless-suppressed_|_always_|_never_++
	*volume* = _0-100_++
	*minimum-interval* = milliseconds between sounds++
	*player* = command, with *{volume}* standing for 0.00 to 1.00++
	*file*, *critical-file* = sound files

*[timeouts]*
	*low*, *normal*, *critical* = seconds until expiry; 0 for never

*[history]*
	*size* = notifications kept

*[do-not-disturb]*
	*on-at-start* = _true_|_false_++
	*critical-sounds* = _true_|_false_

*[app:*_NAME_*]*, matching the application name or desktop entry, ignoring case
	*play-sound*, *urgency* = _low_|_normal_|_critical_, *timeout*, *ignore* = _true_|_false_

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *pw-play*(1), *desktop-shell-system-status-line*(1)
